    {
      "id": "point-supported-distribution-delta-derivatives",
      "type": "exercise",
      "regions": [
        [
          153,
          80,
          485,
          955,
          655
        ]
      ],
      "en": "Assume that the support of the distribution $f$ is the set $\\{0\\}$. Show that $f$ is a linear combination of derivatives of the delta function. Hint: Let $n$ be as given by Lemma~\\ref{lem:distribution-local-finite-order} and assume that $D^\\alpha\\phi(0)$ vanishes for $|\\alpha|\\leq n$. Let $e$ be a test function which equals 1 for $|\\bm{x}|\\leq1$ and 0 for $|\\bm{x}|\\geq2$. Now consider the sequence $\\phi_k(\\bm{x})=\\phi(\\bm{x})e(k\\bm{x})$. Show that $(f,\\phi_k)\\to0$ and hence $(f,\\phi)=0$.",
      "zh": "假设分布 $f$ 的支集为集合 $\\{0\\}$. 证明 $f$ 为 delta 函数的导数的线性组合. Hint: 取 $n$ 如 Lemma~\\ref{lem:distribution-local-finite-order} 所给出, 并假设当 $|\\alpha|\\leq n$ 时 $D^\\alpha\\phi(0)$ 为零. 设 $e$ 为试验函数, 当 $|\\bm{x}|\\leq1$ 时等于 1, 当 $|\\bm{x}|\\geq2$ 时等于 0. 现在考虑序列 $\\phi_k(\\bm{x})=\\phi(\\bm{x})e(k\\bm{x})$. 证明 $(f,\\phi_k)\\to0$, 从而 $(f,\\phi)=0$.",
      "label": "ex:point-supported-distribution-delta-derivatives",
